Z||000007||AusFiero||06-16-2001||04:36 AM||||LOL...and to think he paid to get it done. My mdf console kit has more curves in it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-3_B[1].jpg"> <BR>First lay out your kit. It should have arrived shipped flat. If you notice an curves at all please pack it back up and return it for a replacement kit.<P>Next assemble your mdf body kit using the screws and glue supplied. Do not put to much water in the flour or it will not stick. <P>Get a friend to help you hold it up against the car, if you can find one willing that is.<P>Next mark the position of your body kit with a blunt screwdriver scratching as deeply into the panels as you can as we already know you really have no idea, taste or no how. You bought this kit didn't you.<P>Remove the kit and grab your slegehammer and a screwdriver, they're probably under your trailer or lying around the yard somewhere, look there. How do we know you lived in a trailer? See comment at end of last paragraph. Now take your screwdriver and use it as a punch to make between 2 to 100 holes in the side of the body to hold your panels on. Be sure not to skimp on sledgehammer pressure. A full swing is recommended. <P>At this point you can get the kids involved and get them to smear the flour paste all over the car. Just in case you miss your previously marked lines we decided this was the best method to allow you a small margin for error.<P>Now reposition your body kit and use the 1/4" bolts supplied to bolt it to the car. We didn't give you any washers because we know you wouldn't use them anyway. <P>The glue should be really thickening up by now so stop your rottweiller from eating it , if you can, and use the remaining glue as a body filler to fill any gaps you see between the kit and the car.<P>Let it dry for 20 minutes the grab a paintbrush and any leftover paint you have under the trailer. Mix all the paint together and you now have your new car colour. <P>Don't worry about masking the car up. Get the kids involved again instead and sit back and have a well deserved beer while they finish your masterpiece for you.<P>You will notice the 4 screws under the tail lights. As we know you rarely lift the hood of your car anyway we decided to incorporate a new combined tail light decklid design that just allows you to screw it closed until that day comes that your car just stops and you decide to try fix it. Look at the 7 dissasembled cars behind your trailer first before deciding on this last resort option though.<P>The kids should have the car painted by now so it is time to grab them cool 14" rims you found and replace those big 15" mesh ones you had. We'll show em how to lower a car wont we.<P>Ok all is finished. Do not drive the car no matter how tempting it may be to do so. You bought it to get rich remember. <P>Go inside your trailer and go on the internet. Yes we are assuming you have that too, the 50 foot sattelite dish is gotta be for something right? Log into your E-Bay account and put pictures of your car online and wait for the huge amount of offers you are going to get to start flooding in. \<P>If your car does not sell you have obviously painted it the wrong colour. Raid a neighbours paint stash and try again on e-bay until the car sells and you can afford to buy that Camaro to decorate the front lawn. <P><BR>Sorry...Couldn't help myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
